      "writtenOn": "2026-04-23T17:48:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Can this be flag triggered (even if it\u0027s default true and we add --no-clean or something)? go/rift, for example, ensures the base repo is clean in advance of calling gclient-new-workdir.py and users often only update/clean their base repo once a day, if that, via `rift sync_base --clean`, which implements this functionality, so having this run by default on every new workspace creation would add overhead to invoking this script that\u0027s redundant in that usecase.\n\nIn addition, when calling `rift fork`, it\u0027s actually intended to copy the dirty state of the workspace (which it does by stashing and reapplying diffs) as it\u0027s splitting a workspace so multiple agents can work on a known base state, changed files included.\n\nBy adding a flag to enable or disable the clean behavior, it lets rift (and other tools) disable the feature to lean on the more efficient clean up patterns that are possible with the tool.",
      "revId": "001deccf83804d5a2c1e21613d18067a065e644b",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
